# Commits and Naming

## Conventional Commits

Format: `type(scope): subject`

Types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `test`, `docs`, `chore`, `perf`, `ci`

```
feat(auth): add FirebaseAuthGuard and UserScopedRepository isolation contract
fix(occurrence): return 404 instead of 500 for another user's occurrence
test(recurrence): cover MONTHLY_DAY 'LAST' across leap and non-leap February
```

## Branch naming

- `feature/<ticket-number>-<short-desc>` — new functionality (e.g. `feature/15-main-screen-end-to-end`)
- `fix/<ticket-or-short-desc>` — bug fixes
- `refactor/<scope>` — structural changes
- `chore/<scope>` — tooling, deps, CI

## Semantic naming (mandatory)

Name by **domain and layer**, never generic — and follow each ecosystem's own casing convention rather than forcing one style across both:

```
# ❌ BAD
utils/helpers.ts
common/service.ts
DataProcessor.ts / data_processor.dart

# ✅ GOOD — backend (NestJS, kebab-case + layer suffix)
infrastructure/persistence/user-scoped.repository.ts
infrastructure/auth/firebase-auth.guard.ts
application/users/ensure-user-projection.use-case.ts

# ✅ GOOD — frontend (Flutter/Dart, snake_case)
modules/auth/presentation/bloc/auth_bloc.dart
modules/auth/data/datasources/firebase_auth_datasource.dart
```

## Test coverage

No fixed line-coverage percentage is mandated — this project's testing shape is a decision already recorded in `.scratch/personal-performance-tracker/spec.md`'s **Testing Decisions** section, not an arbitrary number:

- Domain services and value objects (`PerformanceCalculationService`, `RestQuotaPolicy`, `RecurrenceRule`, `TaskRecurrenceHistory`) get pure unit tests, no I/O — this is where most coverage lives.
- Backend integration is **one HTTP seam**, not one test per repository: real requests via `supertest` against a real Postgres (via `testcontainers`), covering cross-user isolation and upsert idempotency. Don't add a bespoke integration test per endpoint/repository beyond that seam.
- Frontend's seam is the **Bloc** (`bloc_test`, events in → states out), not widget tests — except one minimal golden-path widget test per screen for the primary interaction (see `frontend/test/modules/auth/presentation/pages/login_page_test.dart`).
